# French to Brazilian Portuguese Translation & QA Sample: Energy-Inefficient Rental Housing in Île-de-France

## Overview
This repository contains a translation and Quality Assurance (QA) sample from **French (`fr`)** into **Brazilian Portuguese (`pt-BR`)** based on a policy and urban housing text from the *Institut Paris Region* regarding energy-inefficient rental housing (*logements locatifs énergivores*) in Île-de-France.

## Workflow & Tools
- **Translation & Segmentation:** MateCat
- **Quality Assurance (QA) & Terminology Verification:** ApSIC Xbench

## Repository Structure
- `source/` — Original French source text.
- `target/` — Final Brazilian Portuguese target text (adjusted for punctuation, gender agreement, and footnote markers).
- `bilingual/` — Bilingual XLIFF (`.xlf`) file exported for QA inspection.
- `qa/` — QA notes and workflow documentation from ApSIC Xbench.

## Key Translation & Localization Notes
- **Domain Terminology:** Terms such as *diagnostic de performance énergétique (DPE)* and *passoires thermiques* / *logements énergivores* were adapted into natural Brazilian Portuguese housing and energy policy terminology (*diagnóstico de desempenho energético*, *habitações com alto consumo de energia*, and *peneiras térmicas*).
- **Formatting & QA Cleanup:** Removed stray footnote reference digits attached to numbers/words (e.g., `3CL1`, `20262`, `conditions3`), fixed grammatical gender agreement in Portuguese (*Eles permitiram comparar...* referring to *dois workshops*), and standardized title punctuation.
